{"date": "2026-11-10", "word": "Light", "summary": "A light day (forecast moderate). Thermals were strongest (moderate) about 12:00. The upslope ran from about 09:00 to about 15:30. The evening before, the page called it normal, about 5,000 ft, a hit. Midday the base averaged about 5,300 ft by the Kekoa camera, 300 ft higher than the evening's number; the morning update said about 5,300 ft and was right on; at 10:00, from the 09:00 base, about 5,500 ft, off by 200 ft. Most of the day the shear line was crossing Kula Highway near Omaopio; furthest north about 10:22, crossing Kula Highway near Kamehameha Schools; furthest south about 16:50, crossing Kula Highway at the middle Lower Kula Road junction. Data gaps: no readings all day from 1 station (Nakula); Kahikinui stopped at 08:50; Upper Kahikinui stopped at 10:45; the Mesonet could not be reached on 9 of 56 updates.", "therm": "<strong>Light</strong> for the day, 10:00\u201314:00<div class=\"sub\">Kula Ag's measured air through the RRFS sounding (thermal.py); forecast was Moderate</div>", "base": "", "notes": ["Watched for: High base, likely to drop (P6) from 11:37.", "Camera against derived: midday about 300 ft higher, afternoon about 700 ft higher."], "chart": "<div class=\"watch\"><div class=\"kind\">What the day did</div><ul><li>Watched for: High base, likely to drop (P6) from 11:37.</li><li>Camera against derived: midday about 300 ft higher, afternoon about 700 ft higher.</li></ul></div><div style=\"font-weight:600;font-size:.9rem;margin:10px 0 2px\">Cloudbase</div><div style=\"display:flex;gap:14px;flex-wrap:wrap;font-size:.8rem;color:var(--muted,#6b6b66);margin:2px 0 4px\">\n<span><span style=\"display:inline-block;width:16px;border-top:2px dashed #eb6834;vertical-align:middle\"></span> Evening call + usual November day</span><span><span style=\"display:inline-block;width:16px;border-top:2px dashed #8a5cd6;vertical-align:middle\"></span> 10:00 + usual November day</span>\n<span><span style=\"display:inline-b